From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PS3 Linux project <ps3@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:06:30 +0300
Subject: nv30: no second vertex cache invalidate in draws after buffer writes

nv30_state_validate invalidates the vertex cache (0x1710) in every draw, after the last
write any vertex or index buffer of the draw could have had (CPU writes go before the draw
call, coherent mappings included). nv30_draw_vbo then emitted another one, right before the
primitive, whenever a buffer had been written since the last draw (vbo_dirty) or a bound
buffer was mapped coherently, and for the latter walked the vertex buffers every draw to find
out. Nothing writes vertex memory between the two, so the second one invalidated an empty
cache: drop it, and the walk.

Saves two words in the push buffer (and the kernel's copy and check of them) in every draw
that follows a vertex or index buffer write, which with u_vbuf uploading user arrays and
Mesa's immediate-mode buffers is most draws of GL 1.x games, plus the walk over the vertex
buffers in every draw. Changes the command stream: the duplicate 0x1710 is left out; the one
before it stays. Low risk; a hardware test would show stale or corrupt vertices.

NV30_VTX_INVALIDATE_DRAW=1 (read once, at screen creation) emits the draw-time invalidate,
and walks the buffers for it, as before.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_screen.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_screen.c
@@ -523,6 +523,7 @@ nv30_screen_create(struct nouveau_device *dev)
    const bool ps3 = screen->base.is_ps3;
    screen->ps3_vbo_fifo = ps3 && debug_get_bool_option("NV30_PS3_VBO_FIFO", false);
    screen->tex_invalidate_always = debug_get_bool_option("NV30_TEX_INVALIDATE_ALWAYS", false);
+   screen->vtx_invalidate_draw = debug_get_bool_option("NV30_VTX_INVALIDATE_DRAW", false);
    if (!screen->ps3_vbo_fifo)
       screen->base.vidmem_bindings |= PIPE_BIND_VERTEX_BUFFER;
    screen->base.sysmem_bindings |= PIPE_BIND_VERTEX_BUFFER;
